# The leg tag Portable in lit-legs.sh (plan 5.18.10 PX4, P-1a): --portable
# adds the one leg tagged Portable, portable-smoke, to the default set (the
# untagged legs), as --exit adds the Exit legs; --list marks it
# 'portable-smoke (--portable)'. The leg first runs its setup, 'python3
# build-builtins.py --triple msil64-unknown-dotnet' with the build directory,
# and a failed setup is the leg's FAIL row without a lit run. Against the
# stand-in build of Inputs/ci-legs.py, whose lit passes, inside WSL from
# Windows (the WSL legs) and natively on Linux, Inputs/legs-check.py checks:
# (1) --list and --describe name the same legs in the same order, each listed
# with the switch of its tag, and portable-smoke is the one Portable leg.
# (2) The rows (MSIL_CI_RESULTS) of a run with --portable and of one with
# --exit are exactly the legs of that set: --portable takes portable-smoke,
# --exit does not. The stand-in build has no bin/clang, so the real
# build-builtins.py fails the setup (exit 2) and portable-smoke is a FAIL row
# naming its setup log; with the non-lit legs, which the stand-in cannot
# pass, both runs exit 1.
# (3) With a stand-in python3 first on PATH (Inputs/ci-legs.py python3) that
# plays build-builtins.py: 'ok' makes --leg portable-smoke a PASS row whose
# setup ran with the build directory and the portable triple and whose one
# lit invocation passes exactly the paths, params and lit arguments of
# --describe; 'fail' makes it a FAIL row with exit status 1 and no lit run.
# (4) The failure path: portable-smoke untagged fails the --list check;
# planted as Exit it fails the --portable run, which has it, and the --exit
# run, which lacks it; and the --portable rows fail without --portable.
# portable-tag.test checks lit-legs.ps1 -Portable.
# REQUIRES: msil-ci-bash

# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/ci-legs.py setup %t/build

# (1)
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/ci-legs.py sh --distro %{legs_wsl_distro} %t/build -- --list > %t/list.txt
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/ci-legs.py sh --distro %{legs_wsl_distro} %t/build -- --describe > %t/describe.json
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/legs-check.py tags sh %t/list.txt %t/describe.json > %t/1.log
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/1.log "^legs-check: \d+ legs, the list's tags are the JSON's \(.*Portable 1, .*\); Exit legs: " "^legs-check: Portable legs: portable-smoke$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/list.txt "^portable-smoke \(--portable\)$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} lacks %t/list.txt "^portable-smoke-wsl"
# RUN: %{harness_check} missing %t/build/lit-calls.log

# (2)
# RUN: %{harness_check} exits 1 %python %S/Inputs/ci-legs.py sh --distro %{legs_wsl_distro} %t/build MSIL_CI_RESULTS=%t/rows-portable -- --portable > %t/portable.log
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/legs-check.py rows sh %t/describe.json %t/rows-portable --portable > %t/2-portable.log
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/2-portable.log "^legs-check: \d+ rows, the legs of portable; Exit legs among them: none$" "^legs-check: Portable legs among them: portable-smoke$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/rows-portable "^lit-legs\tportable-smoke\tFAIL\t\d+\tsetup failed: build-builtins\.py --triple msil64-unknown-dotnet \(exit 2; \S*portable-smoke\.setup\.log\)$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/build/lit-results/portable-smoke.setup.log "^build-builtins\.py: error: \S*/bin/clang does not exist "
# RUN: %{harness_check} exits 1 %python %S/Inputs/ci-legs.py sh --distro %{legs_wsl_distro} %t/build MSIL_CI_RESULTS=%t/rows-exit -- --exit > %t/exit.log
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/legs-check.py rows sh %t/describe.json %t/rows-exit --exit > %t/2-exit.log
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/2-exit.log "^legs-check: \d+ rows, the legs of exit; Exit legs among them: (\S+, )*ctest-lto(, \S+)*$" "^legs-check: Portable legs among them: none$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} lacks %t/rows-exit "^lit-legs\tportable-smoke\t"

